---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const supportEmail = "pavlovskii.ilya@gmail.com";
const subject = encodeURIComponent("Dice Roller — Privacy request");
const mailto = `mailto:${supportEmail}?subject=${subject}`;
const effectiveDate = "May 20, 2026";
---
<BaseLayout
        title="Dice Roller — Privacy Policy"
        description="Privacy policy for the Dice Roller mobile app: what data is collected, how it is used, and your rights."
>
    <section class="prose max-w-none">
        <h1>Dice Roller — Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><em>Effective date: {effectiveDate}</em></p>

        <p>
            This privacy policy explains what information the <strong>Dice Roller</strong>
            mobile application ("the app") collects, how it is used, and what choices
            you have. The app is developed by <strong>Ilia Pavlovskii</strong> ("we",
            "us", "developer") and is distributed through the Google Play Store and
            the Apple App Store.
        </p>

        <h2>Information we collect directly</h2>
        <p>
            Dice Roller does not require an account, does not ask you to sign in, and
            does not directly collect personally identifiable information such as your
            name, email address, phone number, or precise location. Your roll history
            and settings are stored locally on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>Information collected by third-party services</h2>
        <p>
            The app uses a small number of third-party services that may collect
            information automatically. We use this information only in aggregate to
            keep the app stable, understand how it is used, and to support free
            distribution through advertising.
        </p>

        <h3>Google Play Services and crash reporting</h3>
        <p>
            When the app crashes or encounters an error, anonymous diagnostic data
            (such as device model, operating system version, app version, and a stack
            trace) may be collected by Google Play Services and/or Firebase
            Crashlytics. This data is used to diagnose and fix problems and does not
            include personally identifiable information.
        </p>

        <h3>Firebase Analytics</h3>
        <p>
            The app uses Firebase Analytics (a Google service) to collect anonymous
            usage statistics such as which screens are viewed, which features are
            used, session length, approximate region, device model, and operating
            system version. This information is used to understand how the app is
            used and to prioritize improvements.
        </p>

        <h3>Google AdMob (advertising)</h3>
        <p>
            The app displays advertisements through Google AdMob. AdMob may collect
            and process data including your device's advertising identifier
            (Android Advertising ID / Apple IDFA), IP address, coarse location, and
            interactions with ads in order to deliver and measure advertising. Where
            required by law (for example, under the EU GDPR or the UK GDPR), the app
            will ask for your consent before personalized ads are shown. You can
            change your choice at any time through your device's settings or by
            contacting us.
        </p>
        <p>
            For details, see the
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google
                Advertising policies</a>
            and the
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy
                Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To operate, maintain, and improve the app.</li>
            <li>To diagnose crashes and fix bugs.</li>
            <li>To understand which features are used so we can prioritize improvements.</li>
            <li>To display advertising that helps keep the app free.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use the
            information collected to identify you personally.
        </p>

        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <p>
            The app may request the following device permissions:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Internet access</strong> — required to load advertisements,
                report crashes, and send anonymous analytics.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Vibration</strong> — used to provide haptic feedback when
                rolling, if your device supports it.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The app does not request access to your contacts, photos, microphone,
            camera, or precise location.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
            Dice Roller is suitable for general audiences. The app is not directed at
            children under the age of 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your
            jurisdiction), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
            children. If you believe that a child has provided personal information,
            please contact us so we can take appropriate action.
        </p>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
            Data stored locally on your device (such as roll history and settings)
            remains there until you clear it or uninstall the app. Aggregated
            analytics and crash data are retained by the relevant service providers
            (Google / Firebase) in accordance with their published retention policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            Depending on your jurisdiction (for example, the EU/UK under the GDPR or
            California under the CCPA), you may have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Request access to the data held about you.</li>
            <li>Request correction or deletion of that data.</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent to personalized advertising.</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            To exercise these rights, contact us at
            <a href={mailto}>{supportEmail}</a>. You can also reset or disable your
            advertising identifier in your device's privacy settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
            We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect the
            limited data we process. No method of electronic transmission or storage
            is 100% secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The updated version
            will be posted on this page with a new effective date. Material changes
            will be highlighted in the app or in an app store update note.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions or requests about this privacy policy can be sent to
            <a href={mailto}>{supportEmail}</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
